leftovers_auto: after every finished mow planner.leftovers by itself, armed. Where its passes mow LEFTOVERS_AUTO_MIN m2
at least the mower is sent out again for them (the start_mowing action), once it's idle in its dock with no emergency
and no rain (rain only counts with /mower_logic/rain_mode on). Once a mow: the leftovers' job starts no other. Not
while the MowBite Updater holds the starts (mowbite/hold on the mower's own broker 127.0.0.1:1883, see HoldReader),
nor when the node can't tell whether it does (the parameter hold false: never held).

PLAN_AHEAD_DELAY s after the map or the settings last changed every active mowing area is planned ahead like
planner.plan plans it, so the app's preview and the next mow find their plan at once.

Whatever plans or looks at a plan's shapes (planner.plan, .leftovers, .drive, planner.simulate's planning, mower_logic's
plan_path, planning ahead, the checks after a mow) waits its turn in one worker (Worker), mower_logic's first; the other
RPCs answer at once meanwhile (planner.settings.set counts from the next planning on). How far a planning got goes to
mowbite/planner/progress (retained, through xbot_monitoring, see PlanProgress): {area_id, key (the plan's), running,
stage (angles, spacing, route, mop_up, done; only to show), done of of (growing), started (unix s), elapsed_s,
estimate_s (what that area's last planning took, null before one), error, waiting_n (the jobs waiting in the worker),
waiting (the first WAITING_SHOWN of them in the order they'll run: [{area_id (null: none, or mower_logic's), job (plan,
drive, leftovers, mower, after_mow), rank (mower, asked, after_mow, ahead), ids (the RPC requests waiting for it, none
for the node's own)}]), planned_on (mower, house), remote_why (why not on the house computer after all, null)}, also as
the queue changes when nothing plans.

remote_planning: plans (mower_logic's, planner.plan's, planned ahead; not the leftovers') are asked of a computer in
the house first (mowbite_planner.house, see RemotePlanning): over the mower's own broker, where its hello says it plans
with this code on this stack. The node builds the plan's geometry itself and takes it only where its own checks
(mowbite_planner.remote.refused: its form, check_plan's rules with this body) find nothing; else, when the house
computer says nothing for REMOTE_STALL s or has no plan in REMOTE_TIMES what the area's last planning took, it plans
itself (why in the log and the progress). The planner's no there is its no. The plans mower_logic got stay kept (in
memory and plans_dir) till its job ends (JOB_COMPLETE, JOB_RESET): resuming finds them, wherever they were planned.

angle_increment: every angle_increment_every finished mows (mower_logic's JOB_COMPLETE event) the lanes of every plan
turn that much further (angle_steps, kept in mowbite_planner_angle.json next to settings_file), within an area's
angle_min..angle_max. The mows are counted for all areas at once: angle_increment_every is the one set for all, an
area's own doesn't count. mower_logic's own mow_angle_increment is best left at 0, both add up.

perimeter_direction random: the loops go round ccw or cw at random, drawn again after every finished mow (JOB_COMPLETE,
not the leftovers' job) from the count of all of them (finished_mows, kept there too, planner.angle.reset leaves it),
the same for every area: a plan asked for again before the next one finishes (resuming, a preview) goes the same way.

In a container of its own (OM_PLANNER=external in open_mower_ros) the node ends with exit code 1 when the ROS master
restarts (a new /run_id): the new master doesn't know its service and RPC methods (nor the slic3r planner's), with
the launch file's own_container everything ends and the restarted container registers them again. Its restart policy
has to be on (restart: unless-stopped, see compose.yaml).
